---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description: "I'm a starter theme for Astro.build",
	title: "About",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-6">About</h1>
	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			I'm a smart contract and full-stack developer who's really fascinated by cybersecurity and
			AI-powered malware development.
		</p>
		<p>
			My journey's been anything but straightforward. Growing up, I wasn’t sure what I wanted to do,
			so I chose what felt like the most versatile option at the time, which was business. Back
			then, I actually thought, "I don't want to do anything too technical," which is pretty ironic
			now. I completed my diploma in International Business at Ngee Ann Poly and then got my
			Bachelor's in Commerce (Marketing and International Business) from the University of Auckland.
		</p>
		<p>
			For about three years, I worked in sales, presales, and marketing. It was fun for a while, but
			I started feeling restless. The work became repetitive, and I realized I wanted to be building
			products, not just selling them. In late 2021, I discovered crypto and was immediately hooked.
			I wanted to be part of this world.
		</p>
		<p>
			So I took a leap of faith and enrolled in a Graduate Diploma in Systems Analysis at NUS. It
			was an amazing decision. It landed me a job in crypto, working with smart contracts and
			building dapps.
		</p>
		<p>
			But here's where things got really interesting. I quickly noticed how rampant hacks were in
			crypto. I learned that it's not enough to just build something cool; you have to build
			something safe. This sparked my interest in smart contract auditing, which eventually led me
			down the rabbit hole of cybersecurity.
		</p>
		<p>
			Now I'm convinced we're heading into an era of cyber warfare. Throw AI into the mix, and you
			get AI-powered malware, something incredibly powerful and still so new. Imagine malware that
			can dynamically adapt, learn, and optimize its attacks in real time. I’m excited to dive into
			these challenges, not just because they’re massive, but because they’re an opportunity to make
			a real difference in how we defend against threats.
		</p>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
